erse":10,"english":"Behold, O Laksmana, yonder car stationed in the sky, splendid, furnished with exceeding grace, wonderful, and seeming as if the sun had fallen from the heavens.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.82,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-5-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3004010","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"41fbcf4e31a9a9f921498cccbc5f87252a5575c8ce40f971bf1cd2cd0b4ec7b3","compact":"04544d93e29587356b153cfb5946ce5d4a627839c881074eecbfe409cee5d66e","nasal":"848abc108649a57b38f18397f628c779b62014e6c38ecdefe91e9fcad6829623"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-4-11","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":4,"verse":11,"english":"Behold, O Laksmana, yonder car stationed in the sky, splendid, furnished with exceeding grace, wonderful, and seeming as if the sun had fallen from the heavens. The steeds standing in the sky are for certain those of which we had formerly heard as beionging to Sakra of many sacrifices.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.621,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-5-7","DUTT-3-5-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3004011","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c159a8069806cd9aae18397f6df9953b525af8159e278ed9f0916b0f6fed7ee6","compact":"e789649a45b7d013e2399860dfbab0663d32f5634e7d87d261bdfc71e69a44b6","nasal":"49bdc083ad7a0daa76ac191f307eb615df1cf5ccf85fe6c04e7e890d7cee830f"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-4-12","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":4,"verse":12,"english":"And, you foremost of men, these youths envisioning (the celestial) by hundreds, wearing earrings, and bearing swords in their hands, are broad of chest, have arms resembling bludgeons in size, and are clad in crimson vesture, like to tigers incapable of being approached.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.712,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-5-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3004012","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"86edb22dd3f6a48070365e0e3a213c2edb837a97865d54c3c288f62fa7a8090a","compact":"c34cd57efff97fac3d3c1fb0496ab997871fa7d456d7345c64c8f51aa27d8e99","nasal":"4c5272a5ac93cc87ebc50008379d3c6cc5d4b3bdefd03e1be72dfaebe6fe62ff"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-4-13","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":4,"verse":13,"english":"Over the breasts of all appear chains of blazing sheen; and, O son of Sumitrā, their beauty appears that of five and twenty.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.875,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-5-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3004013","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"aca962f3e725d7089828fe7da4345ad4b54f5ad06326fffb8936002e9becd2d1","compact":"d693d68e4158003b85316a966c6e4ac3571dad06a8f6f39aaf815322559dc243","nasal":"5f0225b6298263f50285e4f03a6b94c1732c4a6e87c52fb600c09b1948c76572"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-4-14","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":4,"verse":14,"english":"And even this is the ever-enduring age of the celestials, as these foremost of men of sweet looks appear.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-5-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3004014","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"364f9ad508d53d9f8faf7e8551912f7161f48296fd8c7e8706ac9eacec3128de","compact":"293747b4da1fe79ca92c267880ff1598845af407d33c3350b6990b8ca24f70a9","nasal":"b31ad1ad37a5f6c5e3ee67eede2941df7ffec10da6f03e1156dbcbef546a9584"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-4-15","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":4,"verse":15,"english":"O Laksmana, stay here awhile with Vaidehi, so long as I do not gather who it is that is in the effulgent car.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.778,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-5-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3004015","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2db4adbc0184e78e213f15c5059d95b2f38146dba023432ad6c9b3a1c309f603","compact":"45c95200c2e94ce553342189e492919a5cc2a0038ce0ef24ee26168f5898bf3d","nasal":"45c95200c2e94ce553342189e492919a5cc2a0038ce0ef24ee26168f5898bf3d"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-4-16","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":4,"verse":16,"english":"Saying to Sumitrās son, Stay here, Kākutstha bent his steps towards Sarabhaiga's asylum.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-5-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3004016","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6fb50a11d30584018d190fdde89025a0bf8dd50100b5baa165afcb6e9b8f9741","compact":"f96f99e425a62a134306528ea93501c01491b895fe4de813ec9c3e6ab5459305","nasal":"71581c3eb7565ec999bc8dce8e52eceb8ca5576a484be0b0398a2ce4bf72201b"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-4-17","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":4,"verse":17,"english":"And seeing Rāma approach, Saci's lord, taking Sarabhanga's permission, addressed the celestials.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-5-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3004017","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e67b9bab057be4e625c7d9f8be4269aac61d7c626a84e66c725162898fc8a732","compact":"60f6d7ebf60eadcb9b977fcc2b3d9913cd06f8011aa322db1ee668f76046c14a","nasal":"49299482392e2c08f96601eb0993638e534247100a61e0f8163ea1e9475cd90c"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-4-18","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":4,"verse":18,"english":"Rāma is coming hither. Do you set out for another place, ere he yet addresses me. He is not fit to behold me (now.)","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.869,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-5-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3004018","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d69d07fcca2f6eac6e7d9ceeaf4d822578eea3ed91d09c02e9b44ad5b3999c53","compact":"9cdf321c3d421c7c214e1a6086a08ff8b8fa78c1aeae20690d33e93884d63b38","nasal":"9cdf321c3d421c7c214e1a6086a08ff8b8fa78c1aeae20690d33e93884d63b38"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-4-19","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":4,"verse":19,"english":"When he shall have vanquished (his foe in fight) and won success, shall I readily show myself to him. He shall have to achieve an act incapable of being achieved by others.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.781,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-5-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3004019","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"50804ff65b85564a2f18f82cee0c18b73dd94955024c8ed196f009e53b20eece","compact":"98668f676d7f1e85d0ebc7c03ec46fd275a18f901d816ddb7e7c85cedf7bde0a","nasal":"2f2686100aee7984783706d73de3a0ce7dc5309373c5fb8f36a0b173a92910e0"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-4-20","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":4,"verse":20,"english":"Then rendering homage to that anchorite and conversing with him, the wielder of the thunderbolt-subduer of enemies-repaired to heaven in a car yoked with steeds.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.667,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-5-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3004020","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3a83b9a51d0c731665cdd4595207974689c6ca62f5db299acbd6e42e4f4a1b81","compact":"55cd20cd35ef424f8ceb2a01da6307807e1f03ceafb83457d388df31b737de74","nasal":"efc238defbd2df1a81a02779c5a2fb7f512849dacd324033b881f14637d9072a"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-4-21","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":4,"verse":21,"english":"When the thousand-eyed one had gone away, Rāghava accompanied by his companions appeared before Sarabhanga in the (Agni-hotra) chamber.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-5-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3004021","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"170920936b418afd0e35f259f414f23cc2625f2fe4742aeb504cf75656094682","compact":"19c05eee6a7e0e5463e6404895d079586c81247124e86a90b4d12ac42d5872f2","nasal":"552571827ae000ca03b90577fe42c05f4696cebcde782aa510b122e8817d69fb"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-4-22","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":4,"verse":22,"english":"Taking his feet, Rāma, Sītā and Lakşmaņa sat down with the permission of the ascetic, who received them and set apart quarters for them.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-5-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3004022","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3f585e57305c854bdc7ec6b0787337bf29ebcc3dde55373adbc8eb7d398de546","compact":"924ffba4f3c332502ff9f65cc27b89b51f547da6391e963adf4f06b0a9a6bb70","nasal":"c8bec2c48b433a342cacc0fa17dd3776269cc6c01f5649e6f9d4741d9c19b4c8"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-4-23","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":4,"verse":23,"english":"Then Rāghava questioned (the sage) concerning the visit of Sakra; and Sarabhanga related everything to Rāghava.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.842,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-5-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3004023","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6c0b670d1f5202f152719a5f44e0293ed22e364250813c61853863960a4b34e3","compact":"6c3481ab69709d1498ea4d268d1df76f014ccbff4e642403272d98c9d08511cd","nasal":"62797fa96209eb500323d6d3f184a820af2190e66fc443b460741f37b72ba71d"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-4-24","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":4,"verse":24,"english":"O Rāma, this bestower of boons wishes to take me to the regions of Brahmā. I have conquered them, incapable of being attained by persons that have not schooled themselves, by virtue of fierce austerities.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-5-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3004024","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5edb51a53f228b2875e60bdfd2835eb7be923838b004e9720116dd71e74a84aa","compact":"49b4b9931fa0aa0d3380ba7c103b8699cb22beafb03f4d945ad96371fb9b727e","nasal":"49b4b9931fa0aa0d3380ba7c103b8699cb22beafb03f4d945ad96371fb9b727e"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-4-25","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":4,"verse":25,"english":"O chief of men, knowing that you were near, I became anxious to go to the minor celestial regions and the supreme heaven (of Brahmā), after I had seen you, righteous and high-souled, who are my dear guest now.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-5-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3004025","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e96c13837091c808390a58fc87e29be1d4665e7c534191513447613ed897a81d","compact":"0e4000448864763cd5ada6633cadeb1430b9c1660caf742841e7a359f7ea5ccc","nasal":"0e4000448864763cd5ada6633cadeb1430b9c1660caf742841e7a359f7ea5ccc"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-4-26","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":4,"verse":26,"english":"O foremost of men, having had a meeting with you, a high-souled prince of righteous nature, I have for aye attained the excellent regions of Brahmã and Nākaprştha. Do you receive them as pertaining to me.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.783,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-5-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3004026","sanskritFile":"Ram03